---
permalink: /cocktails/search.json
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
  WHAT THE "SEARCH FOR ANYTHING" BOX SEARCHES ON A DRINK PAGE -- GitHub issue
  #1050, 2026-09-15. The drinks' half of food/search.json; read that file's
  comment for the shape and the reasoning, which are the same. Fetched by
  assets/js/page-search.js from the box _includes/back-to-index.html renders.

  THE SAME LIST THE INDEX SHOWS. `all_drinks` is assembled exactly as
  cocktails/index.html assembles it -- the gated public collection, plus the
  drafts ONLY under `site.show_drafts`, which _config_local.yml declares and
  production does not (#235). tests/test_rendered_pages.py holds the two lists
  equal in a production build.

  WHAT A DRINK CARRIES HERE. `moods` is the drink's mood list, which the MOOD
  and HASSLE groups both count (one filter with two headings, MANUAL 9.13 --
  the split is taxonomy.yml's `mood_groups`). `ing` is the CARD'S ingredient
  line, label for label, from _plugins/cocktail_card_ingredients.rb: the card
  name is the chip the index's HAS TO HAVE field offers (MANUAL 9.10.1, "cards
  and search read the VOCABULARY"), so a word chosen here is a word the index
  can apply.

  A JOINED "X OR Y" LABEL IS OFFERED AS ITS PARTS -- #1130, 2026-09-20. The
  card prints "cherry brandy or cherry liqueur" as a true fact about the pour,
  and that string names no single HAS TO HAVE chip, so offering it would be a
  result that matches nothing when clicked (the `?ing=` grammar matches a chip
  WHOLE, MANUAL 13.13). #1051 solved that by dropping such a row from this
  feed; this offers `ing.search_labels` instead, which is the same label in
  the pieces a filter can actually apply -- one per generic, from the same
  `card_names` map the chips themselves are built from.

  WHY IT IS BETTER THAN DROPPING THE ROW. A disjunctive `generic` means
  "either would do" (#441), so the drink genuinely answers a HAS TO HAVE
  question about either -- and `buildPool` in cocktail-search.js already adds
  a chip PER GENERIC, so both halves have been clickable on the index all
  along. The box was the one door that disagreed. The Singapore Sling going
  live made it visible: `cherry brandy` and `cherry liqueur` are poured by
  nothing else, so neither word existed in this feed at all, and the drink was
  findable only by name. Two of the three joined pours were quieter and no
  more correct -- Grand Marnier, triple sec, lightly aged rum and clear
  blended rum are all poured alone elsewhere, so the words were here and the
  two drinks that could use them simply did not answer to them.

  IT STILL FAILS OPEN, and the reason is worth keeping because it has bitten.
  The first version of #1051 kept `where: "generics", 1`, which dropped a row
  with no generic at all (`generics: 0`, labelled from its item) and EVERY row
  on a `jekyll serve` started before the plugin gained the field (MANUAL §1:
  plugins are not reloaded). Helen, testing it on 2026-09-15: "Now the only
  things it returns are cocktail names. Please put it back." So the `if`
  below falls back to `ing.label` whenever `search_labels` is missing: on a
  stale server that is exactly the pre-#1051 behaviour, which is imperfect,
  rather than an empty list, which is broken.

  `items_label` IS "recipes" ON BOTH SITES SINCE #1097 (2026-09-15) -- Helen:
  "'Recipes' means recipes across both sites." It said "drinks" here until
  then, as placeholder copy.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign this_site = site.data.sites[page.site_key] -%}
{%- assign groups = site.data.cocktails.taxonomy.mood_groups -%}
{%- assign all_drinks = site.cocktail_recipes -%}
{%- if site.show_drafts -%}
  {%- assign all_drinks = all_drinks | concat: site.cocktail_drafts -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign sorted_drinks = all_drinks | sort: "title" -%}
{
  "site": {{ page.site_key | jsonify }},
  "home": {{ this_site.home | relative_url | jsonify }},
  "items_label": "recipes",
  "groups": [
    {"kind": "mood", "label": "Mood", "param": "mood", "field": "moods", "values": {{ groups.mood | jsonify }}},
    {"kind": "hassle", "label": "Hassle", "param": "mood", "field": "moods", "values": {{ groups.hassle | jsonify }}},
    {"kind": "ingredient", "label": "Has to have", "param": "ing", "field": "ing"}
  ],
  "items": [
    {%- for d in sorted_drinks %}
    {% unless forloop.first %},{% endunless %}{"t": {{ d.title | jsonify }}, "u": {{ d.url | relative_url | jsonify }}, "moods": {{ d.mood | jsonify }}, "ing": [{%- assign _first_ing = true -%}{%- for ing in d.card_ingredients -%}{%- if ing.search_labels -%}{%- for _l in ing.search_labels -%}{%- unless _first_ing %}, {% endunless -%}{{ _l | jsonify }}{%- assign _first_ing = false -%}{%- endfor -%}{%- else -%}{%- unless _first_ing %}, {% endunless -%}{{ ing.label | jsonify }}{%- assign _first_ing = false -%}{%- endif -%}{%- endfor -%}]}
    {%- endfor %}
  ]
}
